llites out of orbit by pointing at the sky and saying &quot;bang&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Conceal a fully functioning fist under your beard!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:10:45-08:00","id":378155,"title":"","content":"A rather bizarre conversation about the base nWoD's size conversion table stopping on &quot;size 7 = grizzly bears&quot; gave rise to this silly master plan:<br /> <br /> Steps for the recipe to making the local Tetrarchy fear the ground upon which your cabal treads:<br /> 1. Run through the wilderness using sense consciousness to detect grizzly bears.<br /> 2. Use Suppress Other's Life on several grizzly bears (because we all know that grizzly bears have a very poor composure save).<br /> 3. Have a matter/life mage turn the grizzly bears into cyborgs.<br /> 4. Have a forces/matter mage allow those cyborgs to shoot laser beams.<br /> 5. Place grizzly bears in twilight with a reverse application of Touch of the Grave on them so they can interact with the material world while invisible and soundless.<br /> 6. Acquire a large freight hauling truck and place this in twilight.<br /> 7. Remove the ceiling of the cargo area of the truck, add a standing platform on top of the storage pen, place all size 7 modified grizzly bears in the storage pen.<br /> 8. have a master matter/life mage cause the truck to become half truck and half grizzly bear.<br /> 9. Roll up on a local pylon and have your strength enhanced mage (at least strength 8 required) hurl the Suppressed Life, ghostly, cyborg, laser equipped, grizzly bears at the nearest seer.<br /> 10. Have the death mage release the Suppress Life spell effecting the thrown bear.<br /> 11. Continue throwing and releasing bears until the requisite amount of violence, destruction, and death has been achieved.<br /> 12. Name both the transportation vehicle and the operation itself: &quot;Bear Force One.&quot;<br /> 13. profit.<br /> <br /> Optional step: Kill the cyborg grizzly bears and resurrect them as zombies (or revenants if your ST allows and you feel particularly ambitious), this confers the ability to name your weapons: &quot;ghostly, zombie, cyborg, laser equipped, grizzly bears.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cautionary note: the UN may decide that this tactic is a war crime under the Geneva Conventions.<br /> <br /> (yes I realize that a wide range of magic could easily counter this tactic, but the idea is still incredibly over the top and fun xD).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 01-22-2015, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T13:25:40-08:00","id":378332,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, you can make the bear walk upright and replace it's forelegs with tiger sharks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T06:43:45-08:00","id":381907,"tit