ar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T22:06:22-08:00","id":401450,"title":"","content":"I agree!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/208132-fun-activities-as-a-mage?p=385161#post385161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> brilliant answer</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T22:17:31-08:00","id":401452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/208132-fun-activities-as-a-mage?p=385120#post385120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called having fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, building off of this, one of the big things I love about this thread is how it taps into one of the big allures of magic. Awakening can be a harrowing experience, and Finding out what's up with the world can be disheartening, but if gaining magic doesn't evoke a certain need to play, at least for a while, then something very important got lost in the process.<br /> <br /> Magic doesn't just fulfill serious desires, it can fulfill silly and simply fun ones too-for better or for worse.*<br /> <br /> *Consequences never go away, and too much fun with magic is a great way to lose Wisdom or royally screw over reality or, worse, people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T01:13:20-08:00","id":401570,"title":"","content":"Looking through the other 1 dot spells, turns out Forces is just awesome when used creatively (I love my Science build)<br /> <br /> Forces 1 - Influence Heat: Redirect opponent's body heat from the limbs to the head. Resisted action versus Stamina. Success deals a Dexterity penalty (the hands and limbs are numb with cold, can't pull a trigger properly), opponent rolls for Stamina. Failure means the opponent suffers from fever (unsure if bashing damage or attribute penalty), Critical Failure results with a heat stroke.<br /> <br /> Forces 1 - Influence Light: Redirect ambient light (or light from a torch or laser) into an opponent's eyes and focus the light into a fine, laser-like beam. Depending on the intensity of the light source, daze or temporarily blind the opponent. Eye protection such as sunglasses or closed eyelids blocks the spell.<br /> <br /> On a side note, if 2e is going to rebalance Forces to make all forces equal, then kinetic energy becomes stupidly useful.<br /> <br /> 2e Forces 1 - Influence Kinetic Energy: Redirect gun recoil into the bullet. Double the bullet speed and improve accuracy with automatic weapons<br /> <br /> 2e Forces 1 - Influence Kinetic Energy: Redirect opponent's bullet velocity in a radial direction (aka explosion)<br /> <br /> 2e Forces 1 - Influence Kinetic Energy: Redirect wind speed into a pinpoint on the opponent's body.<br /> <br /> The list goes on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4652-rising","name":"Rising","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T01:57:59-08:00","id":401656,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Forces was always the swiss army knife of the Arcana and now even more. That said some of the most complex aplications would probably need Reach (say +2 Reach to turn linear to radial direction?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T02:55:22-08:00","id":401696,"title":"","content":"The thing is, those are only the 1 dot equivilents for 2e (as far as we know), but what about the higher dots? Because at 3 dots or more, Gravity is God.<br /> <br /> An example is the Adept spell: Forces 4 - Transform Energy: Convert one form of energy into another form.<br /> The description suggests sound to light or fire to electricity, but consider what happens when you convert electrical energy to gravitational energy.<br /> <br /> You see, there's this curious thing known as the Coulomb Force which describes the force between charged particles. Unlike charges attract and like charges repel.<br /> Now, if you were to convert that Coulomb Force into Gravitational Force, positive ions would no longer repel each other. They can now only attract each other through Gravity.<br /> On its own though, Gravity is the weakest of the 4 fundamental forces (for example a small fridge magnet can defeat the Earth's Gravity).<br /> Now, what happens when you give Gravity the strength of the Coulomb Force? What happens when that SuperGravity isn't resisted by the Electrical repulsion?<br /> <br /> What you have there folks is Core Collapse, or more commonly known as a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypernova\" target=\"_blank\">Hypernova</a>.<br /> <br /> And this isn't even Master rank (no energy was created or destroyed, only converted from one form to another).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4652-rising","name":"Rising","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T03:35:07-08:00","id":401708,"title":"","content":"You are still limited on the quantity/amount/force of energy you can transform. Is doubtful you would manage getting the full force of the Coulomb Force in equivalent gravity. But it would be terrifying.<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, it is an abstraction. If you transform electrical energy you'll need to reference the chart and the equivalencies would probably be on the scale of +1G per step up the chart, so say +5G for a Main Line electrical current. Still useful, but not literally world-breaking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-11-2015, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T04:40:26-08:00","id":401737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rising</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/208132-fun-activities-as-a-mage?p=401570#post401570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking through the other 1 dot spells, turns out Forces is just awesome when used creatively (I love my Science build)<br /> <br /> Forces 1 - Influence Heat: Redirect opponent's body heat from the limbs to the head. Resisted action versus Stamina. Success deals a Dexterity penalty (the hands and limbs are numb with cold, can't pull a trigger properly), opponent rolls for Stamina. Failure means the opponent suffers from fever (unsure if bashing damage or attribute penalty), Critical Failure results with a heat stroke.<br /> <br /> Forces 1 - Influence Light: Redirect ambient light (or light from a torch or laser) into an opponent's eyes and focus the light into a fine, laser-like beam. Depending on the intensity of the light source, daze or temporarily blind the opponent. Eye protection such as sunglasses or closed eyelids blocks the spell.<br /> <br /> On a side note, if 2e is going to rebalance Forces to make all forces equal, then kinetic energy becomes stupidly useful.<br /> <br /> 2e Forces 1 - Influence Kinetic Energy: Redirect gun recoil into the bullet. Double the bullet speed and improve accuracy with automatic weapons<br /> <br /> 2e Forces 1 - Influence Kinetic Energy: Redirect opponent's bullet velocity in a radial direction (aka explosion)<br /> <br /> 2e Forces 1 - Influence Kinetic Energy: Redirect wind speed into a pinpoint on the opponent's body.<br /> <br /> The list goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all fun things, but they shouldn't apply directly like that. Messing with the body heat of someone, for example, would be a life effect. Yes, I know it's heat, and forces messes with heat, but it's a *life* effect. it's messing with a living pattern internally.<br /> OR it's external, then the parts where the heat is redirected from do not feel anything special (it's energy meant to be lost) and the parts where the heat is redirected to will indeed heat... at the pace of the body itself. This would be a minutes-to-hours effect.<br /> The three hypothetical 2e Forces effects would hit closer to home. Aiding the shot is nice, the other would be the opposite effect, creating insane recoil, and the third's just a damage/bull rush spell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:07:24-08:00","id":416475,"title":"","content":"Fun with Gravitomancy <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Create a Gravity-driven Fusion reactor (aka <a href=\"http://www.ccfe.ac.uk/assets/Images/News/MAST_end_of_shot.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">artificial star</a>)</li> <li>Imbue a toilet with antigravity that only activates upon flushing</li> <li>Weaken local Gravity without correcting for the Pressure gradient (don't break hydrostatic equilibrium or else <a href=\"http://youtu.be/qDMUekfOR-E\" target=\"_blank\">this happens</a>)</li> <li>&quot;<a href=\"http://i2.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/564/315/600.gif\" target=\"_blank\">Use the Force, Luke</a>&quot;</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4652-rising","name":"Rising","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:22:25-08:00","id":417309,"title":"","content":"Use Life to shapeshift into a...<br /> <br /> Angel, upon finding someone that needs cheering up. Give them a quick hug, then disappear.<br /> <br /> Fictional character, at a comic/sci-fi/furry convention. Be in-character at all time. At the end, allow a few people to see you teleport/summon a dragon mount/enter a spaceship/etc and leave.<br /> <br /> Alien. Take an empty gas can to an isolated gas station and ask for Earth-fuel in your best B-movie dialogue. Pay with orichalcum, gems, or something appropriately unusual, then leave.<br /> <br /> Adorable fuzzy animal. Find a girl(s) and receive free food and belly rubs.<br /> <br /> Famous dead person, the next time you go to a museum, art gallery, or similar. Pretend to be an impersonator...badly. &quot;Don't be silly, of course Elvis is dead.&quot; (wink wink, nudge nudge.)<br /> <br /> Mostly-human mythological creature, or slenderman if you're feeling unimaginative, and just scare the hell out of people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T04:59:43-08:00","id":417438,"title":"","content":"Matter 4 (maybe 5): Create and manipulate, from your fingertips, a hair-thin wire stronger than steel and sharper t